+# Voicebox Qwen M4
+
+Custom Apple Silicon build based on `jamiepine/voicebox` main at `51f49de`.
+
+## Included changes
+
+- PR #989: one persistent MLX worker for model load, inference, unload, and Whisper.
+- PR #1074: clear MLX allocator and voice-prompt caches on unload.
+- PR #1078: Qwen EOS/runaway guards, bounded decode, retry with smaller chunks,
+  and a 300-character Qwen default chunk size.
+- Conservative Qwen-only leading burst/decay cleanup adapted from PR #1048.
+- A 600 ms silence gap between newline-separated paragraphs.
+- Qwen 1.7B/0.6B are the only TTS choices shown; Russian is the default language.
+- Official-channel automatic updates are disabled so they cannot overwrite this patch set.
+
+Whisper remains available. Model weights are not bundled and are downloaded by
+Voicebox when selected.
+
+## Build on an M-series Mac
+
+1. Install Homebrew and Xcode Command Line Tools.
+2. Double-click **Build Voicebox Qwen M4.command**. If macOS blocks it,
+   right-click it and choose **Open** once.
+
+Terminal alternative: `./scripts/build-macos-arm64.sh`.
+
+The script validates the machine architecture, installs pinned build dependencies,
+runs the Qwen/MLX tests and TypeScript checks, builds the Python sidecars, creates
+the `.app` and `.dmg`, and verifies an ad-hoc code signature.
+Its full output is also saved to `build-macos-arm64.log` for diagnostics.
+
+Because the app is not Apple-notarized, macOS may quarantine a downloaded build.
+Prefer building locally. If Gatekeeper blocks the result, right-click the app and
+choose **Open** once instead of disabling Gatekeeper globally.
+
+## Existing Voicebox data
+
+The upstream bundle identifier is retained, so profiles and generations use the
+same application data location as official Voicebox. Back up important profiles
+before replacing an installed release.
+
+## Diagnostics
+
+If the backend does not start, run the sidecar directly from Terminal and save its
+output:
+
+```bash
+"/Applications/Voicebox Qwen M4.app/Contents/MacOS/voicebox-server" --help
+```
+
+For an MLX smoke test after opening the app, download Qwen3-TTS 0.6B first, clone a
+short Russian sample, generate two short paragraphs, then unload Qwen and Whisper
+from Settings while watching memory in Activity Monitor.
